# Testing Requirements

Every new unit of logic ships with its test in the same PR. No exceptions
for "I'll add tests later" — untested code does not merge to `main`.

## Use cases (domain)
- Plain `flutter_test`, no widget pump, no Firebase.
- Mock the repository interface with `mocktail`.
- Cover: happy path, at least one failure path (e.g., repository throws).

## Repositories (data)
- Test against a faked data source, not real Firebase.
- Cover the mapping logic (DTO → entity) explicitly — this is where bugs hide.

## Bloc (presentation logic)
- Use `bloc_test`'s `blocTest()`.
- Assert the exact state sequence for a given event sequence.
- Cover: loading → success, loading → failure, and any guard conditions
  (e.g., blocking a duplicate submit while already loading).

## Widgets
- One test per meaningful Bloc state the screen renders (loading / error /
  success), using a fake Bloc (`whenListen` / mocked Bloc) — do not re-test
  business logic already covered at the Bloc level.

## Integration
- One `integration_test` per core end-to-end flow (see SRS), run against the
  Firebase Emulator Suite — never against the real `dev`/`prod` project.

## Naming & structure
- Test file mirrors source path: `lib/features/auth/domain/login_use_case.dart`
  → `test/features/auth/domain/login_use_case_test.dart`.
- Test descriptions read as behavior, not implementation:
  `'emits Authenticated when credentials are valid'`, not `'test login'`.

## Coverage bar (Phase 1 targets — see Volume 5)
- Domain ≥ 85%, Data ≥ 70%, Bloc ≥ 80% of transitions, ≥1 widget test/screen.
